{"number": 131, "text": "                     Exercises\n\n\n             62.1\n                     This list of animals and the adjectives traditionally associated with them in British culture have\n                     got mixed up. Put the adjectives into the correct boxes and write sentences using the idioms.\n                     |     | animal    | wrong adjective | right adjective | example sentence\n\n\n                      1      bat        free\n\n                      2      Ox         slippery\n\n                      3      eel        sly\n\n                      4      bird       blind\n\n                      5      fox        strong\n\n\n            62.2\n                     Rewrite these sentences with idioms from the page opposite.\n                       | don’t mind carrying this box. It’s extremely light. The other one was very very heavy.\n\n                       If | were you, | would avoid that restaurant in every possible way. The food is awful.\n                       Millie never misses anything you do in the office. She sees absolutely everything.\n                       | felt completely out of place with my electric guitar among all those classical musicians.\n                       There are hotels completely covering the landscape all along the coast.\n                       She got up late and came down to breakfast looking scruffy and messy.\n            62.3\n                     Answer these questions.\n                     1 Which  animal has a sore head?\n                     2 Which  animal doesn’t like red things?\n                     3 Which animal lives in hell?\n\n            62.4\n                     Use an idiom from exercise 62.3 to complete each sentence.\n                     1 He was very bad-tempered,\n                     2 Her comments  were like ............... —\n                     3        off like\n\n            62.5\n                     Complete  each of these idioms.\n                     L She drove NOMe                       lightning the moment she heard Patrick had arrived.\n                     2 Don’t ask Robert to post a letter. He has a memory like a\n                     3 Everyone could see what was happening. It WaS AS                 as the nose on your face.\n                                                            as sin, that doesn’t mean that they are not good human\n                       beings. We should not judge people by their external appearance.\n            62.6\n                     Use a dictionary of idioms or another good dictionary to find out which as... as... similes are\n                     associated with these things.\n      Cambridge\n                       a pancake\n\n      Dictionary\n                       a brush\n dictionary.cambridge.org\n                       gold\n                       brass\n                       a bone\n\n\n                                                                        English Idioms in Use Intermediate     129", "char_count": 2922, "mean_conf": 84.95, "word_count": 349, "words": [{"text": "62.1", "x0": 266, "y0": 369, "x1": 369, "y1": 409, "conf": 96, "bold": true}, {"text": "62.2", "x0": 258, "y0": 1086, "x1": 363, "y1": 1124, "conf": 96, "bold": true}, {"text": "62.3", "x0": 257, "y0": 1519, "x1": 362, "y1": 1558, "conf": 96, "bold": true}, {"text": "62.4", "x0": 254, "y0": 1793, "x1": 361, "y1": 1832, "conf": 96, "bold": true}, {"text": "62.5", "x0": 253, "y0": 2063, "x1": 358, "y1": 2102, "conf": 96, "bold": true}, {"text": "62.6", "x0": 253, "y0": 2443, "x1": 359, "y1": 2482, "conf": 96, "bold": true}, {"text": "B&-", "x0": 51, "y0": 2540, "x1": 82, "y1": 2577, "conf": 0, "bold": true}, {"text": "Cambridge", "x0": 133, "y0": 2537, "x1": 350, "y1": 2580, "conf": 96, "bold": true}, {"text": "Dictionary", "x0": 133, "y0": 2585, "x1": 330, "y1": 2626, "conf": 96, "bold": true}, {"text": "dictionary.cambridge.org", "x0": 24, "y0": 2669, "x1": 352, "y1": 2696, "conf": 89, "bold": fa